<section id="waiting-for-data">
  <h2>"Waiting for data" and nothing appears</h2>
  <p>This is expected until GitHub sends Distilled an event for a connected repository. There's no backfill, so the dashboard unlocks on your team's next pull request, merge or deployment. On a quiet repository that can be hours or days.</p>
  <p>If your repositories definitely aren't quiet, check the install landed where you think it did:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Confirm the installation completed on the right organisation, and that the repositories you expected were selected. <a href="https://github.com/settings/installations">Your installed apps page</a> on GitHub shows both.</li>
    <li>Confirm the repositories appear in <strong>Settings → Repositories</strong> in Distilled. If they don't, use <strong>Connect GitHub</strong> to update the grant.</li>
    <li>Force the issue with a throwaway pull request:</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>git checkout -b track-with-distilled
git commit --allow-empty -m "chore: check Distilled tracking"
git push -u origin track-with-distilled
gh pr create --fill</code></pre>
  <p>If it shows up within a minute or so, ingest is working and you were simply waiting on activity.</p>
</section>

<section id="no-deployments">
  <h2>Pull requests show up, but deployments don't</h2>
  <p>The usual cause is that GitHub never sees your deploys, or sees them against an environment Distilled doesn't recognise as production.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Does your pipeline create GitHub Deployments?</strong> If yours doesn't, either emit them from CI or switch the repository to release tracking; both are covered in <a href="/docs/deployment-tracking">Deployment Tracking</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Is the environment name recognised?</strong> It must contain <code>production</code>, <code>prod</code> or <code>live</code>. An environment called <code>main</code> or <code>www</code> won't count.</li>
    <li><strong>Was the environment created after you connected the repository?</strong> Environments are discovered at connection time. Re-run <strong>Connect GitHub</strong> to pick up a new one.</li>
    <li><strong>Did the deployment actually succeed?</strong> Only a <code>success</code> state counts.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="missing-window">
  <h2>The 90d or 6m window is greyed out</h2>
  <p>Wider time windows unlock only when you have enough data. Otherwise a six-month chart would be five months of blank space. The menu unlocks itself as your history builds and the "days of data" figure under the repository name tells you how far off you are.</p>
</section>

<section id="repo-missing">
  <h2>A repository isn't in the list</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Not offered when adding?</strong> The GitHub App's access doesn't include it. Use <strong>Connect GitHub</strong> and update the repository selection on GitHub.</li>
    <li><strong>Was there, now gone?</strong> Either it was removed in Distilled, or access was revoked on GitHub. Removals are deliberately sticky: a repository removed in Distilled won't come back through a GitHub-side sync, only by adding it again.</li>
    <li><strong>In the wrong workspace?</strong> Check the workspace switcher in the profile menu before assuming anything is missing.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="install-stuck">
  <h2>The install won't complete</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Are you an organisation owner?</strong> If not, GitHub turns the install into a request that an owner must approve. Nothing connects until they do.</li>
    <li><strong>Did you start from inside Distilled?</strong> The install link carries a token that binds the installation to your workspace. Start from the onboarding screen or Settings → Repositories.</li>
    <li><strong>Stuck on "Preparing GitHub connection"?</strong> Refresh the page; that mints a fresh link.</li>
    <li><strong>Not an owner of the Distilled workspace?</strong> Only owners can connect GitHub. A member sees a waiting message instead.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="stale">
  <h2>The dashboard says "Data stale"</h2>
  <p>The scheduled recompute hasn't run in the last two hours. Headline numbers are queried live and remain correct; the weekly trend charts may lag. If it persists for more than a few hours, email us; that one's ours to fix, not yours.</p>
</section>

<section id="still-stuck">
  <h2>Still stuck?</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@distilledmetrics.com">hello@distilledmetrics.com</a> with your GitHub organisation name, the repository involved, and what you expected to see. If a specific pull request or deployment is missing, include its link. That's usually enough to find the answer immediately.</p>
</section>

